# Line endings are LF everywhere: in the repository and in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git for Windows checks text files out as CRLF by default (core.autocrlf=true), which
# silently breaks anything that compares file content byte for byte. OpenApiDriftIT is exactly that: it
# diffs the generated OpenAPI document against the committed openapi/auth-server.json, so a CRLF checkout
# would fail `mvn verify` on Windows without one character of the contract having changed.
#
# `eol=lf` rather than a bare `text=auto` on purpose: `text=auto` alone normalises to LF *in the
# repository* but still hands Windows a CRLF working copy, which is precisely the case that breaks.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts are LF or they do not run: a CRLF shebang line leaves the interpreter name with a
# trailing carriage return. Covered by the rule above, restated because the failure is so opaque.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Binary files are never normalised.
*.zip binary
*.jar binary
*.png binary
